-review, then round 3 carry-forward), asserts PASS with no qualification, and passed in receipt 0 on d5e37f2.","id":"claude-code/CR2-1","status":"resolved"},{"evidence":"review-findings.js:56-58 counts a re-report as present when raisedBy (per raising report hash) differs from this report, so a same-round re-review re-report by codex counts. Because latest is computed in a full prepass before the closure loop (:68-98), claude's unsupported is blocked regardless of storage order. execution.js:866/873 keeps the raise, re-report and closure refs selected. round-policy.test.js:621-650 runs both individual-review orders and asserts a round-5 FAIL. Both passed in receipt 0.","id":"claude-code/CR2-2","status":"resolved"},{"evidence":"Affected by the rewrite of the prepass. A report's own first raise sets raisedBy without adding to present (review-findings.js:57), so the raising round can still close the finding in a same-revision re-review. round-policy.test.js:553-581 ('a same-revision re-review can close a finding its round raised', round 2 carries the closure with no qualification) passed in receipt 0 on d5e37f2.","id":"claude-code/CR-1","status":"resolved"},{"evidence":"Affected because desktop-projection.json and the desktop mirror changed again this round. Consumed receipt 5 `npm test --prefix apps/desktop` (evaluatedSource d5e37f2, exit 0) ran `npm run stage:protocol` and passed 185/185 tests, including 'Desktop staging contains only self-contained runtime resources' and 'Desktop stages the exact protocol and trusted waiver guard…' (evidence/fc14272a…:3-7, 83, 170, 212-213).","id":"codex/review/desktop-stage-receipt","status":"resolved"}],"findings":[{"blocking":false,"classId":"round-group-perspective-conflation","classStatement":"The per-round perspective map keys only by provider, so another gate's report from the same selection-tagged execution can supersede that provider's review perspective.","criterion":"gate:review","evidence":"review-findings.js:44-63 iterates every history report, including non-review gates, and the second loop only skips non-review at :69. :49-50 derive key and provider from the shared input. :60-62 `perspectives.set(provider, present)` overwrites per provider without the gate. execution.js:985-997 puts one roundPolicy on the input shared by all gates of the execution, and :815 permits review together with code/spec/judge. execution.js latestContext (:849-853) can put such cross-gate reports into history. Before this change, prior review-findings.js:52-58 unioned present sets per key, so it had no such loss. Requires a multi-gate tagged execution, a peer disagreement and a particular storage order, so it is low.","failureScenario":"An individual selection-tagged gate.execute with gates ['review','spec'] (allowed by execution.js:815) stores a review report in which codex re-reports medium regression F, then a spec report from the same input. The claude peer marks F resolved in the same round. Later, the prepass sets latest[key]['codex'] to the spec report's present set, which lacks F. peerPresent therefore returns false and claude's resolved closes F and clears its origin. A later round can then demote F as a non-regression although codex still reports it.","id":"claude-code/CR3-1","path":"repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/protocol/current/review-findings.js","severity":"low"}],"gate":"review","historyAssessment":{"affected":["claude-code/CR-1","codex/review/desktop-stage-receipt"],"carryForwardReason":"codex/review/closed-scope-sweep-reuse is unaffected by the round-3 delta. sweep-records.js, which holds the epoch filter (scopeSweepRecords:87-103), and round-policy.js scopeEpoch are not among the changed regression paths, and the round key in review-findings.js:49 still includes policy.epoch. So the closure (records and round groups of a closed scope never match a later scope with the same name and revision) still applies as verified in round 2, and the sweep-records.test.js:140-156 closed-scope and epoch assertions passed in receipt 0 on d5e37f2."},"mandateAssessment":{"evidence":"Goal (close #144 with AC4 sweep records and cross-round regression tracking): delivered by sweep-records.js, the boundary-review.js roundSchedule hook and the review-findings.js #134 fold-in (DEC-4, recorded as falling naturally out of the change). Constraint 'keep edits to execution.js/boundary-review.js small': the round-3 execution.js edit is limited to the closures[] bookkeeping at :866-907; boundary-review.js adds about 4 lines (:40-47); local-agent-adapters.js is untouched. The disposition shape is extensible for #148 (D1 reversibility notes added values). The verdict-correction policy is respected: GateReeve never sets a reviewer's blocking flag (PROTOCOL.md:734-736). Not merged: the PR is open and unmerged per the tracker. The agent decisions D1-D7 and S2-S11/DEC-2..5 are within the mandate, reversible and recorded. Public PR text is not in the supplied evidence, so the no-local-paths constraint for PR text cannot be checked here. The in-repo docs contain no local paths.","outcome":"PASS"},"outcome":"PASS","summary":"Round 3 (band all-non-low) delta and full feature review of head d5e37f2 against base 6874b9d (target equals base). The round-2 class fix in review-findings.js:43-67 is correct for the claimed scenarios. Each provider's latest report in a (scope, epoch, round, revision) group is its perspective. A re-report counts as present when a different earlier report raised the ID. A closure is blocked only by another provider's latest perspective. In execution.js:866-907, findingStates keeps every closure since the last reopening and puts it in history (closures[]), so a superseding re-review reaches qualification. The new tests (round-policy.test.js:587-650) reproduce CR2-1 and CR2-2 in both orders and pass in the consumed receipt. I found one new low instance of the perspective-conflation class: the prepass keys perspectives by provider only, not by gate, so a multi-gate selection-tagged gate.execute can let a non-review report supersede the same provider's review perspective. It is low and nonblocking. Contextual caveat: a FAIL re-review that omits an earlier-present finding also supersedes it, which is consistent with the documented latest-perspective rule. Sweep records, the scope epoch, claim validation and the regression rule are unchanged since round 2 and still satisfy R1-R5. Docs and the mirror satisfy R7. Local receipts on this tree cover every changed source area, including desktop staging and the --claims help text. The hosted CI plan covers the remainder."}]}